  "details": "There is a glitch that prevents users from turning avatars on or off.\n\nAdditionally, the nameplate does not accurately represent the user's voice state.\n\nPlease refer to the attached video: \n\nhttps://youtu.be/qUhj8gKQOT0\n\nIn this example:\n\nI try to toggle one user's avatar through QM, but the user isn't responding and the avatar isn't actually changing.\n\nI try to adjust the user's volume and mute/unmute them, and that works. But the nameplate doesn't show the updated state with volume % and muted icon.\n\nI try to do the same for different user nearby, and it works like it should: the avatar is toggled on and off, and the name plate shows icons about voice. \n\nYou can also see that the toggled avatar visibility is applied after blocking and unblocking the user.\n\nThis happens for about ~5% of the users. When there's a big crowd in instance of about ~80 people, it looks like 2-4 of them are randomly affected by the glitch. I also noticed that most of affected users are mobile (Android) users, not sure if all of them was mobile.\n\nRe-joining the instance might solve the issue, but it could also lead to the same glitch for different users.\n\nThis happened to me before, about a year ago, and then it got \"fixed\" on its own. Now it's happening again for a few days, currently on build 1750.",
